   $q$What is the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Making a linoleum print takes careful, reverse planning but rewards artists.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Printing presses are better tools than wooden spoons for making prints.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Beginners should avoid using letters or numbers in their designs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A brayer is a rubber roller used to spread ink evenly over a block.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Making a linoleum print takes careful, reverse planning but rewards artists.$q$, $q$The passage walks through the steps of making a linoleum print, stresses thinking in reverse and ends by explaining why students find it rewarding. The brayer is only one tool used in one step.$q$, 'draft', '31c18e49-e861-5c97-8e95-598491c74bb6')
